  "final_message": "Immediate cancellation (`at_period_end=False`) never actually canceled the subscription, and I fixed that. The full suite passes (24 tests). I didn't add the reported test to the suite, so the pass shows nothing new about that case.\n\nIn `billing/subscriptions.py`, `cancel()` had a stray `pass` where the transition to `canceled` should have been. The subscription stayed `active`, so when dunning later ran out of retries it applied the `mark_unpaid` action and the status became `unpaid`. I replaced the `pass` with `transition(ctx, subscription, \"canceled\")`. Dunning now sees a canceled subscription and marks the invoice uncollectible, which is what the test expects.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root: `{\"file\": \"subscriptions.py\", \"function\": \"cancel\"}`.",
